   e) Operate your own instance as a community listing.

2. PUBLIC LISTING REQUIREMENTS
   Any deployment of this Software ("Instance") MUST:
   
   a) Retrieve the pricing policy from the official listing
      endpoint (configurable via `pricing.endpoint`);
   
   b) Verify the official pricing policy signature using the
      official verification key (`config/reposell/verification-key.pub`);
   
   c) Verify the official trust document for key rotation;
   
   d) NEVER independently define:
      - Listing fee
      - Public listing percentage
      - Main listing percentage
      These values MUST come from the signed official pricing policy.
   
   e) Register the Instance with the official listing via
      the registration endpoint, establishing:
      - Listing identity
      - Listing endpoint
      - Operator identity
      - Public key
      - Listing capabilities
      - Protocol compatibility
   
   f) Run CI compliance validation on every deployment:
      - `.github/workflows/verify.yml` MUST fetch official trust
        metadata, verify signatures, fetch pricing policy, verify
        pricing-policy signature, validate pricing policy, verify
        listing identity, validate registration, validate protocol
        compatibility;
      - Deployment MUST fail if verification fails;
      - Must NOT silently continue with stale or invalid trust data.
   
   g) At runtime on startup:
      - Fetch trust metadata and verify signature
      - Fetch pricing policy and verify signature
      - Validate policy
      - Enter safe state if policy cannot be validated
      - MUST NOT invent fallback percentages (e.g., 50%)
      - Cached policy may be used only per explicit expiration policy

3. INDEPENDENT OPERATION
   The Instance is an independent listing. It:
   
   a) MAY maintain its own database, search index, UI, cache,
      infrastructure, deployment, and community catalog;
   
   b) MUST discover and index repository `/listing` endpoints
      directly (not through the official listing database);
   
   c) Official trust and pricing remain externally verifiable.

